{
 "format": "fnv.nif.schema/1",
 "_comment": "The Skyrim family: the NIF layouts the original edition and the Special Edition share. Measured over the original edition's 18,930 meshes; the Special Edition's own differences live in its own directory.",
 "blocks": {
  "NiAVObject": {
   "inherit": "NiObjectNET",
   "abstract": true,
   "fields": [
    {
     "name": "flags",
     "type": "u32"
    },
    {
     "name": "translation",
     "type": "vec3"
    },
    {
     "name": "rotation",
     "type": "mat33"
    },
    {
     "name": "scale",
     "type": "f32"
    },
    {
     "name": "collision_object",
     "type": "ref"
    }
   ],
   "note": "Skyrim's AV object. It has no properties array, where Fallout's has a count and an array; reading them where there are none put every field after the scale a fixed distance off, which is what made NiNode, NiCamera and BSFadeNode fail. A minority of blocks carry a word the reading does not model, and those are the only nodes that still fail."
  },
  "NiTriShapeData": {
